  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "Positive numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) satisfy \\(xy=16\\). What is the minimum value of \\(x+y\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "8",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(x+y\\ge 2\\sqrt{xy}=8\\), with equality attained when \\(x=y=4\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Use a nonnegative difference square\n\nThe product is fixed, so compare the square of the sum with four times the product. Since \\((x-y)^2\\ge0\\),\n\\[\n(x+y)^2=(x-y)^2+4xy\\ge64.\n\\]\nBecause \\(x+y>0\\), this gives \\(x+y\\ge8\\). Equality occurs at \\(x=y=4\\), which satisfies \\(xy=16\\), so the minimum is \\(8\\).",
